What happens if you split the await from the return?

``` js
try {
    const result = await asyncLog();
    return result;
} finally {
    // Do the thing
}
```

@platinumazure That has the same behavior as

``` js
try {
    return await asyncLog();
} finally {
    // Do the thing
}
```

